\define update-risk-actions(threat)
<!--
  update-risk-actions(threat) — recalculate a threat's risk scores.

  CyPro's risk model (per threat):
    risk = impact x probability        (both on a 1..5 scale)
  We track two snapshots of that product:
    - initial_risk : the raw risk before any mitigating measures
    - final_risk   : the risk left after the assigned measures take effect

  Measures linked to a threat store their effect in two per-threat fields named
  "<threatTitle>_RI" (Reduzierung Impact / Schadenshöhe) and "<threatTitle>_RP"
  (Reduzierung Probability / Eintrittshäufigkeit). Those values are stored as
  NEGATIVE numbers (the UI offers 0, -1, -2, -3, -4 — see viewtemplates/threat/
  measures). We SUM every measure's contribution and ADD it to the initial value,
  then floor the result at 1 with max[1] so risk never drops below the minimum.
  (A measure reducing risk = a negative number added, not subtracted.)

  Called as the `actions` of the measure radio buttons and the add/remove measure
  buttons, so the four risk fields stay in sync whenever a measure changes.

  TASK-127 semantics — "unassessed" is not "risk 1": a threat is only assessed when
  BOTH `initial_impact` and `initial_probability` carry a value. If either is blank
  (never rated, or a partially rated threat), the derived fields are CLEARED instead
  of written, so the threat does not appear as a fabricated 1x1. A real out-of-range
  value like `0` is still clamped to 1; only blank means unassessed.

  Note: the math operators treat an empty operand as 0 (multiply) or return the
  operand (add), so a blank source cannot simply "propagate empty" through the
  calculation — an explicit assessed-guard is required (the two $list branches below).

  Parameter `threat` is optional: if blank we fall back to <currentTiddler>, so the
  macro works both when explicitly targeting a threat and when run inside one.
-->
<!-- 1. Compute the values (read fields, derive reductions, clamp) and an `assessed`
     marker (non-empty only when BOTH source fields carry a value). -->
<$let
    tiddler={{{ [<__threat__>!is[blank]then<__threat__>else<currentTiddler>] }}}
    assessed={{{ [<tiddler>has[initial_impact]has[initial_probability]then[yes]] }}}
    reduction_impact_field={{{ [<tiddler>addsuffix[_RI]] }}}
    reduction_probability_field={{{ [<tiddler>addsuffix[_RP]] }}}
    initial_impact={{{ [<tiddler>get[initial_impact]max[1]min[4]] }}}
    initial_probability={{{ [<tiddler>get[initial_probability]max[1]min[4]] }}}
		initial_risk={{{ [<initial_impact>multiply<initial_probability>] }}}
    reduction_impact={{{ [tag[measure]tag<tiddler>get<reduction_impact_field>sum[]else[0]] }}}
    reduction_probability={{{ [tag[measure]tag<tiddler>get<reduction_probability_field>sum[]else[0]] }}}
    final_impact={{{ [<initial_impact>add<reduction_impact>max[1]] }}}
    final_probability={{{ [<initial_probability>add<reduction_probability>max[1]] }}}
    final_risk={{{ [<final_impact>multiply<final_probability>] }}}
>
<!-- 2a. Assessed: write the four derived fields back to the target threat tiddler -->
<$list filter="[<assessed>match[yes]]" variable="null">
<$action-setfield 
    $tiddler=<<tiddler>> 
    initial_risk=<<initial_risk>> 
		final_impact=<<final_impact>> 
    final_probability=<<final_probability>> 
    final_risk=<<final_risk>> 
/>
</$list>
<!-- 2b. Unassessed: clear any stale derived value (no fabricated 1x1) -->
<$list filter="[<assessed>match[yes]] +[count[]match[0]]" variable="null">
<$action-setfield 
    $tiddler=<<tiddler>> 
    initial_risk="" 
		final_impact="" 
    final_probability="" 
    final_risk="" 
/>
</$list>

</$let>
\end